{"question_text": {"৪৯তম বিসিএস ⎯ ফলিত গণিত (৫৬১)": [{"id": "1", "question": "১) <img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceclip0_XHI7ALE.png\" width=\"685\" height=\"53\">", "option1": "Simple zero", "option2": "Zero of order 1", "option3": "Zero of order 2", "option4": "Essential singularity", "answer": "3", "exp": "<p><img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceclip1_rYvxrzZ.png\" width=\"850\" height=\"75\"></p>"}, {"id": "2", "question": "২) Evaluate<br><img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceclip0_iEv1EsZ.png\" width=\"336\" height=\"154\">", "option1": "0", "option2": "<span class=\"mord\">2</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">πi</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">e</span>", "option3": "<span class=\"mord\">2</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">πi</span>", "option4": "<span class=\"mord mathnormal\">πi</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">e</span>", "answer": "2", "exp": "<p><img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceclip1_ckD7Ntf.png\" width=\"450\" height=\"123\"></p>"}, {"id": "3", "question": "৩) The point z = 0&nbsp;is a removable singularity of which function?", "option1": "<span class=\"base\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">f</span><span class=\"mopen\">(</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">z</span><span class=\"mclose\">) </span><span class=\"mrel\">= </span></span><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mfrac\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\"><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\"><span class=\"mop mtight\"><span class=\"mtight\">s</span><span class=\"mtight\">i</span><span class=\"mtight\">n</span></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\">z/z</span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span></span></span></span></span>", "option2": "<span class=\"base\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">f</span><span class=\"mopen\">(</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">z</span><span class=\"mclose\">) </span><span class=\"mrel\">= 1/</span></span><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mfrac\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\"><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\">z</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span>", "option3": "<span class=\"base\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">f</span><span class=\"mopen\">(</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">z</span><span class=\"mclose\">) </span><span class=\"mrel\">= </span></span><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">e</span><sup><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\"><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\">1/<span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\">z</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></sup></span></span>", "option4": "All of these", "answer": "1", "exp": "<p><img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceclip0_ip9gPaJ.png\" width=\"982\" height=\"59\"></p>"}, {"id": "4", "question": "৪) Which of the following has a pole?", "option1": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceclip0_4Vyj4UM.png\" width=\"258\" height=\"86\">", "option2": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceclip1_JYs3f1Q.png\" width=\"238\" height=\"73\">", "option3": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceclip2_za3axuM.png\" width=\"351\" height=\"54\">", "option4": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceclip4_ihYPSDj.png\" width=\"260\" height=\"68\">", "answer": "4", "exp": "<p><img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceclip5_GnRXlMp.png\" width=\"784\" height=\"368\"></p>"}, {"id": "5", "question": "৫) Evaluate<br><img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceclip0_5aqh16L.png\" width=\"375\" height=\"147\">", "option1": "<span class=\"mord\">2π</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">i </span><span class=\"mop\">cos</span><span class=\"mopen\">(</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">i</span><span class=\"mclose\">)</span>", "option2": "<span class=\"mord\">− </span><span class=\"mord\">2π</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">i </span><span class=\"mop\">sinh</span><span class=\"mopen\">(</span><span class=\"mord\">1</span><span class=\"mclose\">)</span>", "option3": "0", "option4": "None of these", "answer": "2", "exp": "<p><img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceclip2_0GAR6y9.png\" width=\"530\" height=\"233\"></p>"}, {"id": "6", "question": "৬) Zeros of a non-constant analytic function are:", "option1": "Always continuous", "option2": "Infinite and accumulating", "option3": "Isolated points", "option4": "Only at <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\">z = 0</span></span>", "answer": "3", "exp": "<p>Non-constant analytic functions cannot have a cluster of zeros accumulating inside the domain (Identity Theorem). Hence zeros are isolated.</p>"}, {"id": "7", "question": "৭) Evaluate<br><img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/1_CWByjuH.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"293\" height=\"173\">", "option1": "<span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"mord\">2π</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">i</span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">e</span><sup><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\"><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\">2</span></span></span></span></span></span></sup></span></span></span></span>", "option2": "<span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\"><span class=\"mord\">π</span>i</span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">e</span><sup><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\"><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\">2</span></span></span></span></span></span></sup></span></span></span></span>", "option3": "0", "option4": "Undefined", "answer": "3", "exp": "<p><img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceclip1_x17TpmZ.png\" width=\"680\" height=\"62\"></p>"}, {"id": "8", "question": "৮) <img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceclip0_sr74qxg.png\" width=\"854\" height=\"66\">", "option1": "Removable", "option2": "Pole of order 1", "option3": "Essential", "option4": "None of these", "answer": "1", "exp": "<p><img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceclip2_CmfdyfJ.png\" width=\"539\" height=\"156\"></p>"}, {"id": "9", "question": "৯) Identify the type of singularity of&nbsp;<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/1_L1p5Mfo.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"268\" height=\"77\">", "option1": "Removable", "option2": "Pole of order 3", "option3": "Essential", "option4": "Simple pole", "answer": "2", "exp": "<p><img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceclip1_IamnpZq.png\" width=\"576\" height=\"37\"></p>"}, {"id": "10", "question": "১০) If&nbsp;<span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\">f(z) = z<sup>2</sup>(z − 1)</span></span>, the number of zeros inside a contour enclosing&nbsp;<span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\">z = 0</span></span>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\">z = 1</span></span> is:", "option1": "0", "option2": "1", "option3": "2", "option4": "3", "answer": "4", "exp": ""}, {"id": "11", "question": "১১) Which singularity does<br><img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceclip0_ifCniNq.png\" width=\"311\" height=\"103\">have at <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\">z=0</span></span>?", "option1": "Removable", "option2": "Simple pole", "option3": "Essential", "option4": "None of these", "answer": "3", "exp": "<p><img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceclip1_xUq89eB.png\" width=\"622\" height=\"184\"></p>"}, {"id": "12", "question": "১২) What type of singularity does<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceclip1_6moWsHx.png\" width=\"264\" height=\"128\">have at <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\">z=0</span></span>?", "option1": "Removable", "option2": "Pole of order 2", "option3": "Essential", "option4": "None of these", "answer": "3", "exp": "<p><img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceclip0_aQHUPxH.png\" width=\"541\" height=\"252\"></p>"}, {"id": "13", "question": "১৩) For<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceclip0_xHv71es.png\" width=\"244\" height=\"123\"><br>the singularity at z = 2 is:", "option1": "Removable", "option2": "Simple pole", "option3": "Essential", "option4": "None", "answer": "1", "exp": "<p><img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceclip1_aqb6Nve.png\" width=\"495\" height=\"99\"></p>"}, {"id": "14", "question": "১৪) Evaluate<br><img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceclip0_pjD7sH2.png\" width=\"300\" height=\"134\">", "option1": "0", "option2": "2πi", "option3": "e", "option4": "πi", "answer": "1", "exp": "<p><img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceclip1_9hSxATb.png\" width=\"526\" height=\"54\"></p>"}, {"id": "15", "question": "১৫) If <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\">f(z)</span></span>&nbsp;is <strong data-start=\"202\" data-end=\"231\">non-constant and analytic</strong> in a domain D, which of the following is true?", "option1": "<span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">f</span><span class=\"mopen\">(</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">D</span><span class=\"mclose\">)</span></span></span></span> may be a single point", "option2": "<span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">f</span><span class=\"mopen\">(</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">D</span><span class=\"mclose\">)</span></span></span></span> is always open.", "option3": "<span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">f</span><span class=\"mopen\">(</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">D</span><span class=\"mclose\">)</span></span></span></span> is always closed.", "option4": "<span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">f</span><span class=\"mopen\">(</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">D</span><span class=\"mclose\">)</span></span></span></span> may contain only real numbers.", "answer": "2", "exp": "<p><img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceclip0_cITwOFr.png\" width=\"618\" height=\"92\"></p>"}, {"id": "16", "question": "১৬) The residue theorem is used to evaluate:", "option1": "Definite integrals of real functions only", "option2": "Line integrals of analytic functions around singularities", "option3": "Improper integrals of trigonometric functions only", "option4": "Derivatives of analytic functions", "answer": "2", "exp": "<p><img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceclip0_zdPKFOn.png\" width=\"525\" height=\"109\"></p>"}, {"id": "17", "question": "১৭) Which of the following statements is <strong data-start=\"445\" data-end=\"453\">true</strong> for zeros of analytic functions?", "option1": "Zeros of an analytic function are always dense in the domain.", "option2": "Every zero must have multiplicity one.", "option3": "Zeros always occur in conjugate pairs.", "option4": "Zeros of an analytic function are isolated unless the function is identically zero.", "answer": "4", "exp": "<p>By the Isolated Zeros Theorem, zeros of a non-constant analytic function are isolated points unless the function is identically zero.</p>"}, {"id": "18", "question": "১৮) If f(z) has a simple pole at z=a, then Res[f(z),a]=", "option1": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceclip0_6x9SWxU.png\" width=\"147\" height=\"79\">", "option2": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceclip1_9RmG5Fe.png\" width=\"221\" height=\"63\">", "option3": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceclip2_yFvrfxW.png\" width=\"231\" height=\"54\">", "option4": "None of these", "answer": "2", "exp": "<p><img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceclip3_bK5AW1h.png\" width=\"429\" height=\"74\"></p>"}, {"id": "19", "question": "১৯) Morera’s theorem is essentially the <strong data-start=\"895\" data-end=\"907\">converse</strong> of which theorem?", "option1": "Liouville’s theorem", "option2": "Residue theorem", "option3": "Maximum modulus theorem", "option4": "Cauchy’s theorem", "answer": "4", "exp": "<p><img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceclip0_BqJy0zf.png\" width=\"539\" height=\"127\"></p>"}, {"id": "20", "question": "২০) Evaluate<br><img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceclip1_mIixYbP.png\" width=\"267\" height=\"137\">", "option1": "0", "option2": "<span class=\"mord\">2π</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">i</span>", "option3": "<span class=\"mord mathnormal\"><span class=\"mord\">π</span>i</span>", "option4": "<span class=\"mord\">4π</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">i</span>", "answer": "1", "exp": "<p><img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceclip3_cJIp2NK.png\" width=\"528\" height=\"369\"></p>"}, {"id": "21", "question": "২১) If <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\">f(z) = z<sup>4 </sup>+ 4</span></span>, then the number of zeros and their order is:", "option1": "4 zeros, each simple", "option2": "2 zeros, each of order 2", "option3": "4 zeros, all at the same point", "option4": "1 zero of order 4", "answer": "1", "exp": "<p><img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceclip0_yGaATn3.png\" width=\"760\" height=\"104\"></p>"}, {"id": "22", "question": "২২) Which of the following integrals equals zero?", "option1": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceclip0_CT1B6QI.png\" width=\"271\" height=\"101\">", "option2": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceclip1_CxbJHTG.png\" width=\"300\" height=\"88\">", "option3": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceclip2_KXC1X4z.png\" width=\"253\" height=\"95\">", "option4": "None of these", "answer": "1", "exp": "<p><img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceclip3_W4ndfoT.png\" width=\"413\" height=\"54\"></p>"}, {"id": "23", "question": "২৩) Contour integration evaluates:", "option1": "Contour integration evaluates:", "option2": "Integrals of complex functions along a path in the complex plane", "option3": "Derivatives of analytic functions", "option4": "Limits of sequences", "answer": "2", "exp": "<p>A contour integral is of the form ∫<sub>C</sub>f(z) dz, where C is a curve in the complex plane. Analytic function theory allows evaluating such integrals using theorems like Cauchy’s theorem and Residue theorem.</p>"}, {"id": "24", "question": "২৪) Evaluate<br><img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceclip1_wGg5UbG.png\" width=\"306\" height=\"124\">", "option1": "0", "option2": "20πi", "option3": "60πi", "option4": "πi/5", "answer": "2", "exp": "<p><img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceclip0_PcLNU0R.png\" width=\"616\" height=\"228\"></p>"}, {"id": "25", "question": "২৫) <img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceclip0_kbMVXtr.png\" width=\"685\" height=\"53\">", "option1": "1", "option2": "5", "option3": "6", "option4": "Infinity", "answer": "3", "exp": "<p><img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceclip1_XLXlXZL.png\" width=\"616\" height=\"129\"></p>"}, {"id": "26", "question": "২৬) Evaluate<br><img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceclip0_MZ9tLum.png\" width=\"314\" height=\"119\">", "option1": "0", "option2": "2πi", "option3": "4πi", "option4": "6πi", "answer": "4", "exp": "<p><img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceclip1_v8B4ols.png\" width=\"615\" height=\"208\"></p>"}, {"id": "27", "question": "২৭) Evaluate<br><img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceclip0_eXEWTLI.png\" width=\"386\" height=\"120\">", "option1": "0", "option2": "2πi", "option3": "8πi", "option4": "10πi", "answer": "1", "exp": "<p><img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceclip1_Ap2fgxh.png\" width=\"700\" height=\"90\"></p>"}, {"id": "28", "question": "২৮) If <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\">P(z) = z<sup>n </sup>+ (lower degree terms)</span></span>, then for sufficiently large <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\">∣z∣ = R</span></span>, the number of zeros inside the circle is:", "option1": "0", "option2": "1", "option3": "n", "option4": "Depends on Coeffivients", "answer": "3", "exp": "<p>For large ∣z∣, the leading term z<sup>n</sup> dominates. By Rouche’s theorem, P(z)) has as many zeros as z<sup>n</sup>, i.e., n zeros inside the circle of radius R.</p>"}, {"id": "29", "question": "২৯) How many zeros of <span class=\"katex-display\"><span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\">P(z) = z<sup>4 </sup>+ 5z + 2 </span></span></span>lie inside <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\">∣z∣ = 1</span></span>?", "option1": "0", "option2": "1", "option3": "2", "option4": "4", "answer": "2", "exp": "<p><img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceclip0_9xq8lyf.png\" width=\"646\" height=\"167\"></p>"}, {"id": "30", "question": "৩০) Use Rouche’s theorem to find the number of zeros of P(z) = z<sup>2</sup> + 3z + 2 inside ∣z∣ = 1.", "option1": "0", "option2": "1", "option3": "2", "option4": "None of these", "answer": "1", "exp": "<p>Factor: P(z)=(z+1)(z+2). Roots: −1,−2. Both lie outside ∣z∣&lt;1. So 0 zeros inside.</p>"}, {"id": "31", "question": "৩১) Evaluate<br><img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceclip0_1v4vHSX.png\" width=\"322\" height=\"104\">", "option1": "0", "option2": "<span class=\"mord\">2π</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">i</span><span class=\"mop\">n</span><sup><span class=\"mord\">2</span></sup>", "option3": "<span class=\"mord\">2π</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">i</span>", "option4": "<span class=\"mord mathnormal\"><span class=\"mord\">π</span>i</span>", "answer": "4", "exp": "<p><img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceclip1_t4l20OI.png\" width=\"568\" height=\"258\"></p>"}, {"id": "32", "question": "৩২) Fundamental Theorem of Algebra", "option1": "Find poles of analytic functions", "option2": "Count the number of zeros of analytic functions inside a closed contour", "option3": "Expand functions into series", "option4": "Evaluate integrals directly", "answer": "2", "exp": "<p>Rouche’s theorem compares two analytic functions f(z) and g(z) on a contour and guarantees they have the same number of zeros inside if ∣g(z)∣&lt;∣f(z)∣ on the contour.</p>"}, {"id": "33", "question": "৩৩) The polynomial&nbsp;<span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\">P(z) = (z − 2)<sup>3</sup></span></span> has:", "option1": "1 distinct root with multiplicity 3", "option2": "2 distinct roots", "option3": "3 distinct roots", "option4": "No roots", "answer": "1", "exp": "<p>P(z)=(z−2)<sup>3</sup> has the single root z=2, but with multiplicity 3. Still satisfies Fundamental Theorem of Algebra, as total number of roots = degree = 3.</p>"}, {"id": "34", "question": "৩৪) A cubic polynomial&nbsp;<span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\">P(z) = z<sup>3 </sup>- 1</span></span>&nbsp;has how many roots in&nbsp;<span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\">C</span></span>?", "option1": "1 root", "option2": "2 roots", "option3": "3 roots", "option4": "6 roots", "answer": "3", "exp": "<p><img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceclip0_APmVz9C.png\" width=\"602\" height=\"107\"></p>"}, {"id": "35", "question": "৩৫) Evaluate<br><img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceclip1_Q7Bduwr.png\" width=\"306\" height=\"122\">", "option1": "0", "option2": "1", "option3": "2πi", "option4": "None of these", "answer": "1", "exp": "<p><img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceclip2_TZeuaS1.png\" width=\"792\" height=\"70\"></p>"}, {"id": "36", "question": "৩৬) If&nbsp;<span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\">f(z)</span></span>&nbsp;is analytic in a simply connected domain&nbsp;<span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\">D</span></span>, then for any closed contour&nbsp;<span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\">C</span></span>&nbsp;in&nbsp;<span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\">D</span></span>", "option1": "<span class=\"base\"><span class=\"mop\"><span class=\"mop op-symbol small-op\">∫</span><sub><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\"><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\">C</span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span></span></span></sub></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">f</span><span class=\"mopen\">(</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">z</span><span class=\"mclose\">)</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">d</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">z </span><span class=\"mrel\">= </span></span><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">f</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\"><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\">′</span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mopen\">(a</span><span class=\"mclose\">)/2πi</span></span>", "option2": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceclip1_rH3KK7r.png\" width=\"210\" height=\"41\">", "option3": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceclip0_5ip0q08.png\" width=\"234\" height=\"44\">", "option4": "None of these", "answer": "3", "exp": "<p>Direct result of Cauchy’s Theorem.</p>"}, {"id": "37", "question": "৩৭) Which statement is correct?", "option1": "Taylor series allows negative powers of&nbsp;<span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\">(z−z<sub>0</sub>)</span></span>", "option2": "Laurent series requires the function to be analytic at <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\">z<sub>0</sub></span></span>", "option3": "Laurent series allows negative powers in an annulus around a singularity", "option4": "Taylor series is valid only for functions with singularities", "answer": "3", "exp": "<p>Taylor series: only non-negative powers, valid inside a disk where f is analytic.<br>Laurent series: allows negative powers in an annulus around isolated singularities.</p>"}, {"id": "38", "question": "৩৮) If <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\">f(z